+<!-- Generated by scripts/docs/generate-forge-claims.ts. Do not edit; run pnpm docs:claims. -->
+# @oods/mcp-bridge
+
+HTTP transport for the native Forge server. Build the server first, then run `pnpm --filter @oods/mcp-bridge run dev` from the repository root. The extracted portable runtime also includes this bridge and its policies.
+
+The default listener is `127.0.0.1:4466`; `MCP_BRIDGE_PORT` overrides the port. `BRIDGE_TOKEN` enables the `X-Bridge-Token` header. Write-gated calls use `X-Bridge-Approval` according to policy. Endpoints are `GET /health`, `GET /tools`, `POST /run` and `/artifacts/*`; refresh `/tools` for the live enabled surface. Build revision and availability are reported by health.
+
+The registry advertises 19 tools by default and 5 on demand (24 total). Enable on-demand entries with `MCP_TOOLSET=all` or select them with `MCP_EXTRA_TOOLS`.
+
+The retained portable adapter E2E exercises 19 advertised tools: 17 results and 2 typed dependency limits, brand.apply (OODS-N020) and design.preview (OODS-N019). Source evidence tiers below do not imply executed proof for every tool.
+
+| Default tool / actions | Source evidence tier |
+| --- | --- |
+| `tokens.build` | product-reality |
+| `structuredData.fetch` | product-reality |
+| `brand.apply` | product-reality |
+| `brand.intake` | product-reality |
+| `catalog.list` | product-reality |
+| `code.generate` | product-reality |
+| `design.compose` | product-reality |
+| `design.preview` | product-reality |
+| `pipeline` | product-reality |
+| `health` | product-reality |
+| `registry.snapshot` | product-reality |
+| `viz.render` | product-reality |
+| `dashboard.render` | product-reality |
+| `artifact.certify` | product-reality |
+| `fidelity.preview` | product-reality |
+| `map` (`create`/`list`/`resolve`/`update`/`delete`/`apply`) | product-reality |
+| `schema` (`save`/`load`/`list`/`delete`) | product-reality |
+| `object` (`list`/`show`) | product-reality |
+| `repl` (`render`/`validate`) | product-reality |
+
+| On-demand tool | Source evidence tier |
+| --- | --- |
+| `diag.snapshot` | contract |
+| `billing.reviewKit` | contract |
+| `billing.switchFixtures` | contract |
+| `a11y.scan` | contract |
+| `release.tag` | contract |
+
+Retired tools and their rationale are recorded in the generated [Tool-Specs retirement table](../../docs/mcp/Tool-Specs.md).
+
+The extracted-bundle reference-app ledger records 42 cells for Organization, Subscription and User across 7 contexts and react and vue: 42 pass, 0 typed gaps and 42 generated artifacts equal their host hashes. These bounded receipts do not imply universal application coverage.
+
+Sources: [tool registry](../mcp-server/src/tools/registry.json), [tool ledger](../mcp-server/registry/tool-capability-ledger.v1.json), [release ledger](../mcp-server/registry/release-cells.v1.json). Complete contracts: [Tool-Specs](../../docs/mcp/Tool-Specs.md), [API reference](../../docs/api/README.md). Connection profiles: [Connections](../../docs/mcp/Connections.md). Extracted distribution: [portable runtime](../../docs/runtime/portable-runtime.md).
